      ],
      "impact": "The CAN buses lose their specified ESD/transient protection, and placing slow single-ended optocouplers in the high-speed differential CAN pair corrupts/attenuates the signaling, likely rendering CAN0/CAN1 non-functional or unreliable against motor-controller traffic.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN protection path deviates from the intended design: the spec-mandated CDSOT23-SM712 TVS arrays on D9/D10 are absent and those references instead carry dual optocouplers wired into the CAN0/CAN1 differential pairs, removing ESD protection and corrupting the CAN signaling."
}

